  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for safe work, accurate readings and the ability to troubleshoot. They judge you by projects, notes and safety discipline.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is reading a circuit diagram and writing a clear note on it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and job oriented courses for EEE students: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools simulate circuits and draft reports. Routine documentation shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Safety judgment, hands-on troubleshooting and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explain and check; later, own designs and decisions.
  </p>

