  <h2 id="eeediag">Reading a single-line diagram, step by step</h2>

  <p>
    A single-line diagram shows how power moves from source to load using one line for three phases. Reading it well is a basic skill that most power and maintenance roles expect.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Step</th>
          <th>What to find</th>
          <th>Question to ask</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>1</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to find">The source and its rating</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">How much can it supply?</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>2</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to find">Transformers and their ratios</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">What voltage changes happen here?</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>3</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to find">Breakers and protection</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">What trips first in a fault?</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>4</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to find">Feeders and loads</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">Which loads share a line?</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>5</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to find">Earthing points</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">Where is the path to ground?</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="money">Money: course fees and the 10 percent test</h2>

  <p>
    As a rule of thumb and not a research finding, keep a degree or course fee near a tenth of the family's total education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a serious caution that needs course-specific evidence.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 8 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 80,000 for the main course, and a fifth is Rs 1.6 lakh as a serious caution. The rest can fund a laptop, practice time and a reserve.
  </p>
  <p>
    Test the field with free courses and one finished project before paying for a long programme. Do not borrow heavily for a course whose graduates cannot show placement in a specific role.
  </p>

